  "analysis": "The reviewer recounts a card-album completion system and one paid purchase made inside it. The album is a collection of collectible cards that awards a grand prize when completed; the player was two cards short of finishing. A purchased 'deal' was expected to deliver the missing new cards but instead returned useless duplicates, which the reviewer calls a scam and warns others against. The mechanics visible in the account: a collection-completion goal near its end, a real-money purchase whose delivered cards come from a pool in which duplicates occur, and the near-complete state of the album motivating the spend. The 'brain-rot / Free Cash' remark concerns out-of-game promotion of the game and is outside scope (R13), and 'DON'T GET IN-APP PURCHASES' is an evaluation rather than a mechanic on its own.",
  "labels": [
    {
      "label": "P_CompleteTheCollection",
      "span": "I had two cards left which would grant me the grand prize for completing an album",
      "rule_applied": "Definition: 'drives players to feel compelled to acquire all in-game items, achievements, or myths'",
      "rationale": "The reviewer is working toward finishing a card album and made a purchase specifically to obtain the last two cards for the grand prize, showing the collection-completion structure in action."
